From: harunkkhan <harunkkhan1@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Present the passkey sheet on the tab's own window

macOS's passkey sheet (iCloud Keychain, Touch ID) needs an NSWindow to attach
to, which Chrome finds through the tab's views widget. EngineCore's tabs sit in
AppKit windows with no widget, so the request had no window and the sheet
could not be shown. The tab's top-level native window is used when there is
no widget.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_authenticator_request_delegate.cc b/chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_authenticator_request_delegate.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_authenticator_request_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/webauthn/chrome_authenticator_request_delegate.cc
@@ -1256,6 +1256,13 @@
     if (window) {
       discovery_factory->set_nswindow(window);
     }
+    return;
+  }
+  // EngineCore's tabs sit in AppKit windows with no views widget; the passkey
+  // sheet is presented on the tab's own window.
+  const gfx::NativeWindow window = web_contents->GetTopLevelNativeWindow();
+  if (window) {
+    discovery_factory->set_nswindow(window);
   }
 }
 void ChromeAuthenticatorRequestDelegate::ConfigureICloudKeychain(
